nny line can intersect \\(T_n\\) in at most one point.  \nTherefore the \\(n\\) sunny lines together can cover at most \\(n\\) points of \\(T_n\\).  \nBut \\(|T_n|=\\frac{n(n+1)}{2}>n\\) for every \\(n\\ge 3\\).  \nConsequently some point of \\(T_n\\) would remain uncovered, contradicting the requirement.  \nThus \\(k=n\\) is impossible.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### Conclusion\n\nFor every integer \\(n\\ge 3\\) the set of admissible numbers of sunny lines is exactly  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\{0,1,2,\\dots ,n-1\\}} .\n\\]\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
